    {"dot":"cyan","title":"B02c scope (settings & entitlements)","items":["Modules: department, global-setting, settings-catalog, entitlements, resource-subscription (~47 routes est., completes B02).","Department: admin departments + GET :id/users. Settings: global settings (tenant scope/reveal/rotate) and settings catalog/effective/features/action-confirmations/registry write endpoints under /admin/settings.","Entitlements: admin enabled/plans/tenant overrides/downgrade/trial-expiry plus GET /tenants/me/entitlements. Resource subscriptions: CRUD + toggle under /admin/resource-subscriptions."]},
    {"dot":"violet","title":"Example input/output (representative)","items":["Global setting reveal/rotate: POST :id/reveal or :id/rotate -> revealed/rotated secret metadata (value exposure policy applies).","Settings registry/features: GET effective/features/matrix or PUT matrix/registry key -> resolved/effective settings or updated registry/feature state.","Entitlements override/downgrade: PUT/DELETE tenant override or POST downgrade -> effective plan/override state; /tenants/me/entitlements returns resolved entitlements.","Department/resource subscription: CRUD DTOs -> department/subscription records; toggle changes active state. Verify exact DTO schemas and secret handling."]},
    {"dot":"emerald","title":"Evidence and limitations","items":["Repo https://github.com/ArcaAI/project-hope.git @ 8cb2e5e8e6bbddf5ee7c676782ebb5ad683c23a0. Controller/service sources verified in local tree.","Downstreams: config/entitlement data store (Postgres/Prisma). Feature availability/entitlement enforcement is represented as policy/enforcement; actual runtime checks may be distributed.","Limitations: grouped endpoint nodes (11 controllers across 5 modules); settings-catalog service layering is summarized via EffectiveSettings/Registry/FeatureAvailability services; reconcile exact route contracts and secret redaction behavior for strict contracts."]}
